course: dictionary
lesson: 3690
title: Flash: a quick bright light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word flash can mean different things, so the words around it help you choose. A flash is a quick bright light. To flash is to shine for a very short moment, or to shine on and off. «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang shows whether the storm is coming closer or moving away.» Here the flash is lightning.
explain: Look for phrases too. «In a flash» means very quickly, and «flash by» means to move past very fast. A flash on a camera is a bright light that helps you take photos in the dark. Each time, try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the sentence tells you the idea without using the word again. «Each kind with its own flash code» means each kind of firefly has its own pattern of light. When you see a word you know in a new place, ask: does my meaning fit here?
fact: A flash is a quick bright light.
fact: Lightning is a giant flash, and you see the flash before you hear the thunder.
fact: Light reaches you almost instantly, but sound travels only about 1 kilometre in 3 seconds.
fact: Fireflies are beetles that make cold light in their tails, and each kind has its own flash code.
fact: In the US, a flashlight is what we call a torch in Britain.
exercise: «Counting the seconds between the flash and the bang shows whether the storm is coming closer or moving away.» In this sentence, what is a flash? | *A bright light from lightning | A kind of cloud | A loud crash of thunder | A slow walk in the rain
exercise: Lightning is a giant flash, and you see the flash before you hear the thunder. Why do you see it first? | Lightning only happens when your eyes are closed | *Light reaches you almost instantly, but sound is much slower | Thunder is quieter than lightning | Thunder is a kind of light
exercise: «In a flash» means what? | Brightly, for a long time | In a dark room | *Very quickly | Very slowly
test:  The camera gave a flash, so the photo came out bright in the dark. What is a flash on a camera? | A dark picture | *A bright light to help take photos in the dark | A kind of camera lens | A slow photo with no light
test: «Each kind with its own flash code» means each kind of firefly has its own what? | A special name for the beetle | A loud sound | A secret password | *A pattern of light flashes
exam: «The bus flashed by the window.» What does flashed by mean? | *Moved past very fast | Was painted in bright colours | Stopped suddenly outside the window | Came back slowly
